  "test_file": "tests/test_marine_impulsor_options.gd",
  "scope": "Source-bounded Impulsor scope: exact one-model composition, first-to-third and fourth-plus source price tiers, exact 100 mm circular base and characteristics; complete source keywords and fixed weapon profiles; all one-of systems, Storm Bolters replacement and Heavy Stubber option with reversible public choices, owner/stale rejection and Orbital Comms surcharge; Orbital Comms Scouts 6 and Shield Dome 5+ invulnerable effects; transport capacity and model exclusions; Rapid Disembarkation after Advance; Core Deadly Demise D3 and Firing Deck 7 source parameters; current-catalog admission for both players. Shared transport suites cover Firing Deck attack planning and the Emergency Disembark to Deadly Demise allocation continuation using a Rhino fixture.",
  "limits": "The common-book export and current Wahapedia page are the source boundary. The local construction catalog currently limits Impulsor to three copies while retaining the source fourth-plus cost tier; this is a local catalog gate, not a full army-legality claim. The source lists no common-book Leader or Support relation for Impulsor. Firing Deck 7 and Deadly Demise D3 are checked as Impulsor source bindings, while shared resolution behavior is exercised through the transport suites. Chapter-book content, full faction/army legality, network behavior, complete-match certification and human playtesting remain outside this result; network validation is deferred to final integration.",
  "verification": {
    "command": "python tools/verify.py --godot .tools/godot/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64_console.exe --profile targeted --only test_marine_impulsor_options --only test_marine_transport_profiles --only test_marine_transport_admission --only test_marine_transport_rules --only test_marine_transport_weapon_options --only test_marine_transport_destruction --only test_marine_firing_deck --only test_marine_conditional_weapon_traits --only test_space_marine_leader_links --timeout 300",
    "result": "passed",
